Z||000031||Will||11-28-2000||02:27 PM||||I checked in the Lumina shop manual and a shop manual with the 3.4 pushrod. The cam journal diameters are not the same. The TDC cams must need larger lobes because they don't have 1.5:1 rocker arms increasing the lift.<P>300 degrees and 0.410 ?!? That's quite a cam for the street... <BR>What lobe separation did you use for that 275 HP figure? Where did you get your flowbench numbers?||||reg||1
Z||000032||lowCG||12-12-2000||07:36 PM||||MS,I used Desktop Dyno,don't know anything about the other program.I know that the one I have is based on thermodynamics,and values that different changes have on this.The results have been pretty accurate.<BR>The cam profile I used was one that's very popular with Fiat 4 cylinder twincams,and is very streetable when used with individual runner intakes. ||||reg||1
